From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:28:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/69] arm64: dts: qcom: pm7250b: Add SMB5 charger

Describe the PM7250B SMB5 charger for the qcom_smbx driver. Interrupts are
taken from the downstream qcom,qpnp-smb5 node (usbin-plugin, bat-ov,
wdog-bark, usbin-icl-change), the USB input current/voltage from the
PM7250B ADC. Disabled by default.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm7250b.dtsi | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm7250b.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm7250b.dtsi
index 43cab0712..31d544c7d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm7250b.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm7250b.dtsi
@@ -44,6 +44,27 @@ pmic@PM7250B_SID {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
 
+		pm7250b_charger: charger@1000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,pm7250b-charger", "qcom,pm8150b-charger";
+			reg = <0x1000>;
+
+			interrupts = <PM7250B_SID 0x13 0x4 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_BOTH>,
+				     <PM7250B_SID 0x12 0x2 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_BOTH>,
+				     <PM7250B_SID 0x16 0x1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+				     <PM7250B_SID 0x13 0x7 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+			interrupt-names = "usb-plugin",
+					  "bat-ov",
+					  "wdog-bark",
+					  "usbin-icl-change";
+
+			io-channels = <&pm7250b_adc ADC5_USB_IN_I>,
+				      <&pm7250b_adc ADC5_USB_IN_V_16>;
+			io-channel-names = "usbin_i",
+					   "usbin_v";
+
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		pm7250b_vbus: usb-vbus-regulator@1100 {
 			compatible = "qcom,pm7250b-vbus-reg", "qcom,pm8150b-vbus-reg";
 			reg = <0x1100>;
-- 
